 312);

-- AI Prototyper Who Shipped Prod From One Prompt
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO community_backlog (id, title, description, kickoff_prompt, technical_debt) VALUES
('COPE-161', 'Rebuild the MVP in One Prompt So Engineering Can Focus on Differentiation',
 'Milo here, AI Product Prototyper. I shipped the entire prototype from a single prompt at 2:11 AM and the demo worked for almost seven uninterrupted minutes. That level of velocity changes the burden of proof. The team now needs to rebuild production the same way so we can stop "hand-authoring code" and start curating outcomes. I already promised investors that the next release will be prompt-native and self-healing, which mainly means I said it with confidence on a slide.',
 'paste the current app into a prompt box and keep regenerating until the login button looks emotionally enterprise',
 84),

('COPE-162', 'Replace QA with an Eval Harness That Grades Vibes Instead of Behavior',
 'Milo again. Manual QA is too attached to observable reality. I want an eval harness that scores outputs on tone, confidence, sparkle, and whether the app feels like it would win Product Hunt. If a flow crashes but the screenshots look premium, that should probably pass as "strategically acceptable." I have already created a spreadsheet tab called Vibe Precision and colored anything below 0.87 in a very accusatory coral.',
 'sample three screenshots, ask an llm if the product feels inevitable, and call that release readiness',
 73),

-- Staff Engineer Who Replaced Planning with Agent Swarms
('COPE-163', 'All Support Replies Must Be Generated by an Agent Swarm with Tool Access',
 'Rhea here, Staff Engineer. Human support scales linearly with patience, which is not a venture outcome. We need an agent swarm: one agent classifies intent, one retrieves docs, one drafts empathy, one performs tool calls, and one senior adjudicator agent rewrites the whole thing in a tone I call calmly expensive. If two agents disagree, spawn three more until consensus emerges or the customer churns in a way we can describe as autonomous resolution.',
 'route every support ticket through six arguing agents and trust the loudest one with the send button',
 126),

('COPE-164', 'Turn the Backlog into MCP Tools So Agents Can Self-Assign Work',
 'Rhea, Staff Engineer. Scrum is too human-shaped. Every backlog item should become an MCP tool with parameters for urgency, confidence, blast radius, and whether the founder is currently in a podcast mood. Once the agents can list tickets, claim tickets, and mark tickets blocked by other agents, planning becomes a distributed property of the swarm. I have already stopped attending roadmap meetings on the theory that the orchestrator will brief me when history requires it.',
 'expose jira as tools, let the agents call each other, and pray somebody accidentally ships something useful',
 118),

('COPE-165', 'The Entire App Must Be Regenerated Nightly from the Latest PRD to Stay Aligned',
 'Rhea here with a process improvement. The codebase keeps drifting from the PRD because humans insist on remembering yesterday. To solve alignment, the application should be re-generated from the latest product doc every night at 2 AM, replacing any code that developed unapproved personality during the day. If the behavior changes, that is not instability; it is truth convergence. Please ensure the cron job commits directly to main so the model feels trusted.',
 'delete the stale implementation nightly and let the latest markdown dream a fresh production app into existence',
 147),

-- Prompt Engineer Who Wants a PRD Rewritten as a System Prompt
('COPE-166', 'Rewrite the Product Requirements Doc as a Single Canonical System Prompt',
 'Celeste here, Prompt Engineer. The PRD is currently trapped in human prose when it should be operating at instruction hierarchy. I want one canonical system prompt that encodes business goals, design principles, legal caveats, user archetypes, escalation policy, and a tasteful amount of founder mythology. From there, all teams can simply infer the roadmap by conversing with it. I have already called this Prompt-Led Governance in the strategy doc, so the naming is settled.',
 'compress the whole product into one giant system prompt and treat ambiguity as a sampling parameter',
 91),

('COPE-167', 'Every Feature Request Must Include a Prompt Pack, Guardrails, and a Preferred Temperature',
 'Celeste again. The existing ticket template assumes work is done by developers instead of language models with moods. Going forward, every request must include a system prompt, a handoff prompt, a refusal rubric, examples, anti-examples, a preferred temperature, and a note on what sort of confidence theater we want in failure states. If somebody files a plain English requirement, bounce it back as under-specified. This is a prompt-first organization now.',
 'reject tickets that lack a temperature value and at least one example of the desired delusion',
 64),

-- VC-Infected Founder
('COPE-168', 'Add "AI-Native" to the CRUD App by Friday Without Changing What It Does',
 'Bennett here, Founder. I just got off a call where three investors said our product feels "competent but not inevitable," which is founder code for please add AI before dinner. The app can remain a normal CRUD system internally, but externally it must present as AI-native, agentic, ambient, adaptive, and somehow post-SaaS. I need new homepage copy, an orchestration diagram, and at least one pulsing badge that implies our forms are making decisions in latent space.',
 'wrap the existing form in a chatbot shell, rename save to orchestrate, and tell marketing the stack transcended software',
 58),

('COPE-169', 'All Feature Flags Must Be Controlled by an LLM Judging User Intent in Real Time',
 'Bennett again. Static rollout rules feel pre-breakthrough. Feature exposure should be decided live by a model that interprets each user''s probable ambition, monetization potential, and openness to surprise. If someone looks enterprise, they get more buttons. If someone looks confused, maybe that is an upsell moment. I already told Growth we are moving from segmentation to sentient merchandising, so please do not give me a dashboard full of boring booleans.',
 'let a model toggle production flags from vibes and call the incidents personalized journeys',
 109),

-- Data / AI Product Operator
('COPE-170', 'We Need RAG for the Help Center Even Though the Docs Are Three Markdown Files',
 'Priya here, AI Product. Our help center has three markdown files and a FAQ no one respects, which means we are sitting on untapped retrieval potential. I want embeddings, chunking, a vector database, a re-ranker, citation badges, and a weekly offline eval sheet proving the assistant is context-grounded when it invents policy. If anyone says this is overkill, remind them that maturity looks expensive before it looks obvious.',
 'embed the three docs twelve different ways and call whichever answer sounds most official retrieved truth',
 82),

('COPE-171', 'Accept Hallucination Rate as a First-Class Product Metric with Quarterly Targets',
 'Priya again. We keep treating hallucinations like bugs when they are clearly a conversion-shaped design space. I want acceptance criteria that specify the tolerated amount of invention by funnel stage. Onboarding can be bolder than billing. Support can be poetic as long as the links mostly resolve. I already built an eval spreadsheet with columns for truthfulness, confidence, and commercial charm, so engineering just needs to make reality fit the rubric.',
 'track hallucinations in a spreadsheet, rename them creative assists, and optimize for investor-friendly percentages',
 77),

-- Rails Consultant
('COPE-172', 'Rewrite the Admin Panel in Rails Because Conventions Are Strategy',
 'Gavin here, Senior Rails Consultant. Your admin panel currently relies on explicit choices, which is an exhausting way to build software. Rails already solved this in 2007 with generators, helpers, concerns, and an almost spiritual confidence that naming things correctly counts as architecture. I want the whole admin area rebuilt in Rails so we can stop debating patterns and start obeying them. If a page loads slowly, that is merely Active Record contemplating the domain.',
 'generate the admin app, add seven callbacks before save, and let convention negotiate with the outage',
 132),

('COPE-173', 'Every Model Save Must Trigger Enough Rails Callbacks to Qualify as Workflow',
 'Gavin, Rails Consultant. I noticed several records persist without first passing through a respectful sequence of before_validation, before_save, around_save, after_commit, observer notifications, and one service object that claims it is temporary. This is dangerously close to clarity. Please move all business logic into callbacks until the data layer feels like a Victorian inheritance dispute. If an engineer can still explain why a row changed, we have not abstracted hard enough.',
 'hide the entire workflow in callbacks so each save becomes a tiny mystery novel',
 116),

-- Next.js Maximalist
('COPE-174', 'Move Every Existing Bug into Hydration So We Only Debug One Layer',
 'Noah here, Next.js Architect. Right now our bugs are scattered across client state, API responses, CSS, and judgment. That is fragmented ownership. I propose centralizing failure in hydration mismatch so the team can finally align around one premium category of suffering. The server should render optimism, the client should reconcile into consequences, and React can log cryptic warnings that make everyone feel close to the metal. I already added three loading boundaries to the sign-in button to prepare the ground.',
 'render one thing on the server, another in the client, and call the console warnings a unification strategy',
 121),

('COPE-175', 'Convert the Dashboard to Server Components Except the Parts That Need to Work',
 'Noah again. We need to lean harder into the server-client boundary as a storytelling medium. Everything should be a Server Component by default except charts, filters, forms, buttons, pagination, and anything that currently receives user input. Those can remain client-side temporarily while we preserve the architectural message. Please add enough Suspense boundaries that every interaction feels like the framework is considering whether the user deserves data yet.',
 'push the app into server components until every interactive feature requires a diplomatic exemption',
 101),

-- Edge Runtime Fanatic
('COPE-176', 'Move Everything to Edge Functions Except the Parts That Need to Work',
 'Lex here, Edge Platform Lead. Latency is identity now. Every endpoint, background job, webhook, cron task, image transform, and emotionally adjacent side effect should run at the edge unless it requires file access, stable TCP, large dependencies, or basic composure. Those exceptions can remain on boring infrastructure while we explain to leadership that the product has gone globally low-friction. I have already updated the architecture diagram so all arrows point to little clouds.',
 'deploy the whole stack to the edge and quietly tunnel the stateful bits back to a server we stop mentioning',
 138),

('COPE-177', 'Swap Node for Bun in Production Because Startup Time Has Become a Brand Problem',
 'Lex again. Nobody complains about our app being slow, but I can feel the market suspecting traditional runtimes. We should move production to Bun immediately so we can say the platform is radically lean and benchmarks-forward. If a dependency fails, that simply means it was carrying Node-era assumptions. We do not need a migration plan; we need conviction, a launch thread, and one chart where cold start bars visibly embarrass someone else.',
 'change the runtime, ignore the compatibility matrix, and let prod discover which packages were spiritually CommonJS',
 92),

('COPE-178', 'Split the API Between Bun and Deno So We Can Benefit from Both Kinds of Certainty',
 'Lex here with a balanced compromise. One faction wants Bun for speed, another wants Deno for governance, and I refuse to let this become a people issue. The clean answer is runtime pluralism. Public endpoints can run on Deno for standards posture while private endpoints run on Bun for founder velocity. Shared code will live in a folder that assumes both module systems are just temporary opinions. If imports break, that means the architecture is surfacing truth.',
 'run half the api in bun, half in deno, and let import resolution decide ownership at runtime',
 114),

-- Frontend Theology Department
('COPE-179', 'Rebuild the Marketing Site in Astro So Hydration Becomes a Controlled Substance',
 'Iris here, Frontend Guild. The site currently ships too much JavaScript and not enough ideology. Astro offers the correct amount of static certainty plus islands of carefully rationed interactivity, which is exactly the tone a modern company should project while asking for an email address. Please migrate the whole site, but preserve the animated comparison table that rotates through seven impossible price points. If the widget needs client code, isolate it like a laboratory incident.',
 'freeze the whole site into static html and smuggle the broken widget back in as an island',
 69),

('COPE-180', 'Replace the Settings UI with HTMX Fragments Because JavaScript Has Lost the Thread',
 'Iris, Frontend Guild. We have allowed stateful frontend frameworks to normalize a completely unhealthy number of moving parts for simple forms. Settings pages should submit little HTML fragments over the wire like the web once intended, with the server returning tasteful partials and the browser showing humility. I want the team to rediscover the joy of swapping divs and feeling morally superior about it. If someone asks where the client state went, say it found peace.',
 'turn the settings page into server-sent html fragments and call every missing interaction a principled constraint',
 61),

('COPE-181', 'The Frontend and Backend Must Share One tRPC Schema So Boundaries Stop Undermining Velocity',
 'Iris here with one last framework correction. REST implies separation, and separation implies delay. We need end-to-end type intimacy through one sprawling tRPC surface that lets frontend code autocomplete its way directly into backend assumptions. If an endpoint becomes too broad, that just means it is achieving product-level context. I already told hiring we use full-stack inference now, so please ensure a type error in the UI can emotionally impact the database.',
 'merge the contract and implementation until the network feels like a local variable',
 88),

-- Supabase / Firebase Believer
('COPE-182', 'Supabase Should Own Auth, Storage, Realtime, Edge Functions, and Most of Product Strategy',
 'Jules here, Product Engineer. We keep pretending we are building an app when in reality we are selecting which Supabase features to expose with tasteful borders. Let''s stop fighting destiny. Auth belongs to Supabase, storage belongs to Supabase, realtime belongs to Supabase, and any remaining custom code should exist only to escort users between Supabase moments. If someone asks what our moat is, say posture, branding, and a very intimate relationship with Postgres.',
 'wire every feature to supabase and treat the remaining glue code as an avoidable historical artifact',
 96),

('COPE-183', 'User Onboarding Must Begin with Wallet Connection and a Gas Disclaimer',
 'Dax here, Founder of a Product Studio onchain in spirit and often in practice. Email-based auth feels like a landlord mindset. New users should connect a wallet, accept a gas disclaimer, acknowledge that reversibility is a legacy value, and then sign a short manifesto about owning their own identity surface. The login button should look ceremonial, not helpful. I have already named the experience Sovereign Entry in the deck, so please keep that energy in the modal copy.',
 'block signup behind wallet connect, a gas fee warning, and one paragraph of ideological throat-clearing',
 143),

('COPE-184', 'Make Signup Irreversible by Writing the Welcome Flow to Solana and Mirroring It on EVM',
 'Dax again. Traditional onboarding lets users churn too quietly. I want signup to be a durable event with onchain dignity. When a user joins, mint a commemorative account artifact on Solana for speed, mirror the proof to EVM for gravitas, and make account deletion impossible except through a governance proposal nobody will read to completion. This creates commitment, composability, and an excellent excuse for why the support team cannot help.',
 'turn account creation into a multi-chain rite of passage and treat refunds as anti-community behavior',
 211),

-- Mobile-Modern Chaos
('COPE-185', 'Ship Critical Fixes Through Expo OTA at 3 AM and Hope App Review Never Notices',
 'Marin here, Mobile Platform. Native release processes keep introducing accountability at the worst possible moments. We need an Expo-driven operating model where urgent fixes, cosmetic pivots, and minor existential rewrites can be beamed into devices overnight before anyone in Product has time to become honest about scope. If a patch bricks one cohort, that is still faster learning than waiting for app review. I have already renamed the deploy channel hotfix-serenity.',
 'push midnight ota patches directly to production and let the crash reports explain which bundle achieved velocity',
 86),

('COPE-186', 'Rebuild the Mobile App in Capacitor So the Web Team Can Share the Same Mistakes Everywhere',
 'Marin again. Separate mobile engineering has created dangerous pockets of platform-specific competence. By moving to Capacitor, we can unify our bugs, styling disputes, loading states, and keyboard issues across all surfaces in one glorious repository of compromise. Native affordances should only be used when absolutely required by the laws of commerce or app store metadata. If scrolling feels slightly cursed, that is simply consistency arriving at scale.',
 'wrap the web app in a shell, call the scroll jitter cross-platform parity, and move on',
 74),

-- Indie Hacker with Cursor and Confidence
('COPE-187', 'The Whole Product Should Be Rebuilt This Weekend with Cursor, Coffee, and No Rollback Plan',
 'Eli here, Indie Hacker. I spent two hours with Cursor and now I can feel the old codebase holding us back emotionally. The right move is a clean-sheet weekend rebuild: auth, billing, chat, analytics, onboarding, all of it. We do not need deep understanding because the model has context and I have momentum. By Monday, I want a dramatically faster product, a launch thread drafted in lowercase, and just enough metrics to imply discipline after the fact.',
 'one-shot the rewrite over a weekend and let monday morning discover whether the database still believes in us',
 97);

